// @emit-error value-call union-ARM parameter given a value that is not that arm
// THE FLOOR D196 MADE NECESSARY, and it is here so the reject cannot silently become
// invalid wasm again.
//
// `const c = { r: 7 }` is un-annotated in a union program, so `globalKind`'s `ObjLit` arm
// gives it the union BOX. `lamc`'s parameter is the bare ARM, and `emitCallRef` has a
// `union`-parameter arm (`emitUnionBoxArg`, which BOXES an un-boxed member) and no
// `variant`-parameter one — so the box was pushed raw into a `(ref $uVarHeap[vi])` slot.
//
// UNTIL D196 THIS PROGRAM NEVER REACHED THE CALL SITE: the `(Circle) => Circle` annotation
// keyed a struct row that does not exist and `fbValtype`'s bounds guard rejected one stage
// earlier (`ref valtype with no interned shape`). Repairing the key moves the disagreement
// from the type section to the argument — the D52 half-fix shape — and exactly one census
// cell of 250,238 (`cellsB/b000061.vl`) went `loud emit reject` -> `check-clean invalid
// wasm` before this floor was added. A cell moving INTO silence is a blocker whatever its
// count.
//
// THE DIRECT-CALL SPELLING OF THE SAME THREE LINES RUNS — replace the lambda with
// `function idc(x: Circle): Circle { x }` and the box is handled — so this is a value-call
// ABI gap, not an arm-resolution one. D200 is the row; flip this file to `@run` when the
// value call learns to build the arm.
//
// AN `ObjLit` EXEMPTION WAS BUILT HERE AND A WITNESS REFUTED IT. The reasoning was that
// `exprVariantIndex` has no object-literal arm by design, so a bare `f({ r: 7 })` would be
// rejected needlessly; the evidence offered was "the corpus is byte-identical with the
// exemption in place". That evidence proved NOTHING — the corpus contains no program in this
// family at all (D201), so it could not have contained the disagreement. Built as a program,
// `f({ r: 7 })` with an arm-typed closure parameter and NO layout twin went `loud emit
// reject` -> `check-clean invalid wasm` under the exemption: a cell falling INTO silence,
// which is the exact failure this floor exists to prevent. `arm-param-value-call-objlit-arg-
// floor.vl` is that witness, kept beside this one.
//
// THREE SHAPES REACH THIS FLOOR, and each is check-clean INVALID WASM without it: an
// un-annotated binding that reps as the BOX (this file), a bare object LITERAL argument
// (the file beside it), and an `is Circle`-NARROWED union binding passed straight in
// (`function m3(s: Shape) { if s is Circle { f(s) } }`). All three are LOUD on `1e81b0f3`
// too — the floor restores the reject the `$fnsig` repair removed, it does not invent one.
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq
const c = { r: 7 }
const lamc = (x: Circle) => x
const dd = lamc(c)
if (dd).r == 7 { print(7) } else { print(0) }
